# `d[i][0] * d[i][1]`, `d` a parameter of which its uses alone say what it is: the loop is built twice behind a guess at `d`, and each row is asked in its turn.
# One odd row, a row with a text in it, sends the rest of the loop to the other copy. That copy keeps its guesses open: it tests each row for a list of numbers and reads it by that,
# as the loop did before it was built twice; closed, it read every element and multiplied through stubs.
